{#
  TAQATHON - CERTIFICATE VERIFICATION PAGE (src/pages/verify.njk)
  -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Deliberately standalone: this page does NOT extend layouts/base.njk
  and doesn't use the shared navbar/footer partials or common.css —
  it never did, even in the original site. It's meant to be a fast,
  minimal page someone lands on after scanning a QR code printed on a
  physical certificate, not a page for browsing the rest of the site.
  Migrating it into the shared layout would add navigation chrome that
  was intentionally never part of this page's design, so it keeps its
  own full HTML shell here instead — including this redesign (Phase 3,
  editorial rollout, page 16 of 16, the last one): the visual system's
  colors are hardcoded directly into this page's own <style> block
  rather than reading common.css's custom properties, matching this
  page's existing self-contained pattern rather than breaking it.

  VISUAL SYSTEM: only the color values changed (the old blue/green
  brand gradient → this system's cream/terra/amber palette, Tajawal
  for the Arabic display heading). Certificate-status colors
  (valid=green, invalid=red, missing=amber) are UNCHANGED — those are
  universal status semantics, not this page's brand accents, and
  swapping them for on-brand colors would just make "valid" vs
  "invalid" harder to read at a glance for no real gain.

  SECURITY NOTE (not fixed by this migration on purpose): the
  CERTIFICATES object below ships every certificate record — real
  names, roles, dates — to anyone who views this page's source, and
  "verification" is just a client-side object lookup with no integrity
  check. That's a known issue already tracked as its own piece of work
  (moving this to a real lookup: a Google Sheet as the data store, an
  Apps Script endpoint as the API, so the browser only ever receives
  the ONE certificate being looked up). This redesign's job is only
  the visual skin — the certificate registry and every line of lookup
  logic below are untouched.

  TO CUSTOMIZE (until the Phase 1 rework lands):
    - Add/edit certificates → the CERTIFICATES object in the script
      block below, same as the original file.
#}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="ar" dir="rtl">
<head>
